  "self_repairs": [
    "An earlier draft of the core hardcoded MEASURED_SCALAR = 0. The authority's own state_names order is ['STRUCTURALLY_UNMEASURED','MEASURED_SCALAR','MEASURED_COLLISION_UNRESOLVED'], so measured is code 1. The inverted constant would have treated every structurally unmeasured address as measured while discarding genuinely measured ones, inverting the exact distinction this layer preserves. Verified empirically against FOUNDATION_SUPPORT_ADDRESS_RECURRENCE.csv for 2,000 addresses, then bound via load_observation_state_codes.",
    "A weighted-quantile test asserted a median of exactly 3.0 for a skewed-mass fixture. The mid-point empirical definition gives 2 + 50/50.5 exactly. The implementation was correct and the expectation was wrong; it was replaced with the analytic value plus a step-sense check rather than a loosened tolerance.",
    "The AUTHORITY_DEPENDENT_TESTS declaration omitted an authority-dependent test. The AST meta-test caught it, which is why that meta-test exists."
